# Copy to .env.local (development) or set at build time (Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables).
# Set ONE of the two pairs below. Every key here is public by design; NEVER put a service_role / secret key here.

# A) One site for every client (the shared Vercel project behind *.getquicksales.com).
#    The address picks the client: sapcongo.getquicksales.com → the database the control project lists for "sapcongo".
#    Both values are the CONTROL project's: Settings → API. See control/README.md.
VITE_CONTROL_URL=https://YOUR-CONTROL-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
VITE_CONTROL_ANON_KEY=YOUR-CONTROL-ANON-OR-PUBLISHABLE-KEY
# VITE_TENANT_DOMAIN=getquicksales.com      (the default)
# VITE_DEV_TENANT=sapcongo                  (only for `npm run dev` on localhost: which client to open)

# B) One client only (local development, tests, or a site of its own). When set, it wins over A.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-KEY
